ydrolysis in a confined aqueous microenvironment.\",\n      \"reaction_sequence\": [\"rxn_001\", \"rxn_002\", \"rxn_004\", \"rxn_005\", \"rxn_006\", \"rxn_009\"],\n      \"key_intermediates\": [\"mol_005\", \"mol_010\", \"mol_011\", \"mol_012\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P7\",\n      \"name\": \"Patel branch with Cu-assisted aldehyde formation, Cu-assisted homologation, and surface hydrolysis\",\n      \"description\": \"The most copper-intensive Patel variant in this network: copper assists both the aldehyde-forming reduction and the final homologation to the arginine alpha-aminonitrile precursor before surface hydrolysis.\",\n      \"reaction_sequence\": [\"rxn_001\", \"rxn_002\", \"rxn_004\", \"rxn_005\", \"rxn_007\", \"rxn_008\"],\n      \"key_intermediates\": [\"mol_005\", \"mol_010\", \"mol_011\", \"mol_012\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P8\",\n      \"name\": \"Patel branch with Cu-assisted aldehyde formation, Cu-assisted homologation, and compartment hydrolysis\",\n      \"description\": \"Copper-assisted surface precursor chemistry throughout, with the final aminonitrile hydrolyzed after concentration in a biochemical-style pool or compartment.\",\n      \"reaction_sequence\": [\"rxn_001\", \"rxn_002\", \"rxn_004\", \"rxn_005\", \"rxn_007\", \"rxn_009\"],\n      \"key_intermediates\": [\"mol_005\", \"mol_010\", \"mol_011\", \"mol_012\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P9\",\n      \"name\": \"Speculative Orn-first branch from Cu-free beta-aminopropionaldehyde generation\",\n      \"description\": \"After Cu-free sulfide photoreduction to the amino aldehyde, a speculative unguanidinated homologation gives ornithine, which is then guanidinated by cyanamide in a concentrated aqueous microenvironment.\",\n      \"reaction_sequence\": [\"rxn_001\", \"rxn_002\", \"rxn_003\", \"rxn_010\", \"rxn_011\"],\n      \"key_intermediates\": [\"mol_010\", \"mol_013\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P10\",\n      \"name\": \"Speculative Orn-first branch from Cu-assisted beta-aminopropionaldehyde generation\",\n      \"description\": \"The same Orn-first logic as P9, but the amino aldehyde is produced by the Cu-assisted sulfide-photoredox variant before speculative homologation and cyanamide guanidination.\",\n      \"reaction_sequence\": [\"rxn_001\", \"rxn_002\", \"rxn_004\", \"rxn_010\", \"rxn_011\"],\n      \"key_intermediates\": [\"mol_010\", \"mol_013\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"hub_molecules\": [\"mol_005\", \"mol_010\", \"mol_011\", \"mol_012\"],\n  \"convergence_points\": [\n    {\n      \"molecule_id\": \"mol_005\",\n      \"incoming_reactions\": [\"rxn_002\"],\n      \"outgoing_reactions\": [\"rxn_003\", \"rxn_004\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"molecule_id\": \"mol_010\",\n      \"incoming_reactions\": [\"rxn_003\", \"rxn_004\"],\n      \"outgoing_reactions\": [\"rxn_005\", \"rxn_010\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"molecule_id\": \"mol_011\",\n      \"incoming_reactions\": [\"rxn_005\"],\n      \"outgoing_reactions\": [\"rxn_006\", \"rxn_007\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"molecule_id\": \"mol_012\",\n      \"incoming_reactions\": [\"rxn_006\", \"rxn_007\"],\n      \"outgoing_reactions\": [\"rxn_008\", \"rxn_009\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"molecule_id\": \"mol_014\",\n      \"incoming_reactions\": [\"rxn_008\", \"rxn_009\", \"rxn_011\"],\n      \"outgoing_reactions\": []\n    }\n  ]\n}", "parsed_response": {"target_molecule": "Arginine", "overall_strategy": "Prioritize the strongest Arg-specific evidence. The backbone is a surficial cyanosulfidic network because Patel et al. (2015) provide the clearest de novo route from simple feedstocks to the experimentally characterized arginine alpha-aminonitrile; Cu-assisted and Cu-free photoredox variants are represented separately, and free arginine is reached by lower-confidence hydrolysis of that precursor. A secondary Orn-first module is retained because Orn-to-Arg guanidination is chemically strong, but its ornithine-supply step is explicitly marked speculativ